# .cursorrules — ARES-PATH // GALE-01 Project Guidelines

# Project Identity
You are working on "ARES-PATH // GALE-01", a planetary GIS and Marswalk route planner for NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.
Primary Target: Mount Sharp (Aeolis Mons), Gale Crater, Mars (Lat: -5.4453°, Lon: 137.8414°), focusing on Curiosity 2025 boxwork formations.

# Branding Constraints (ZERO NASA LOGOS)
- NEVER download, embed, or render official NASA meatball or worm logos.
- Use only the custom vector mission emblem: `/images/ares-path-badge.svg`.
- Citations must be text-only (USGS, JPL Mars Trek, AMMOS MMGIS, NASA Worldview).

# UI Design Rules (ZERO GRADIENTS, ZERO EMOJIS)
- ZERO GRADIENTS: No bg-gradient-*, linear-gradient, radial-gradient, or glow shadows. Flat solid backgrounds (#07090e, #0b0f17, #111827) and crisp 1px borders.
- ZERO EMOJIS: Never use Unicode emojis in UI text, labels, buttons, or badges. Use monochrome SVG icons or bracketed badges like [SAFE], [CAUTION], [HAZARD].
- TABULAR NUMBERS: Use `font-mono tabular-nums` for all telemetry, coordinates, and percentages with explicit units (m, km, deg, tiu, mSv/sol, L/min, kg).

# Core Models & Engines
- 4 Scientific Layers: Optical & Geologic, Topographic & Hazard (<15°, 15-25°, >25°), Thermal ATI & CT (Morgan et al. 2020), Radiation RAD & REMS.
- Prospector ML Scorer: Promise Score (0-100%) and Model Uncertainty Index (±%).
- Earth Analogue Matcher: Real-time dynamic priority weight sliders matching Haughton, Death Valley, Rio Tinto, Atacama.
- Marswalk A* Router: Terrain-aware least-cost route for Solo Astronaut vs Paired Crew + Mule Rover.
- Offline-First: Always keep local GeoJSON fallbacks active.
